on gain, safety calculations, authorization state, robot trajectory, quantum and classical raw measurements, structured residuals, model forks, resets, abstentions and human overrides into one replayable evidence object. A quantum measurement qualifies only when it reduces biological sampling burden or improves mechanism discrimination against the best classical readout. Architecture Element Contents Core coupling biological digital twins \u00d7 active microsampling \u00d7 quantum-trusted sensing Research lineage Extension of the microrobotic sampling and quantum biosensing mother monograph Mathematics 30 large gold script derivations linked to chapters and Research Gates Main text 82 chapters with five independent single-page research units each Future research 200 detailed Research Gates and 33 Phoenix Answer Embryos Release logic pass fail abstain degrade stop with six-stage QA Edition scale 774 A4 pages and approximately 101,142 English words Scientific Boundary A biological twin is not the biological system itself. Its recommendations must expose mechanism non-uniqueness, parameter identifiability, model discrepancy, extrapolation domain, missing data, physical reachability, ethical and authorization limits, and explicit abstention conditions. If a wrong twin can still trigger a high-risk action, the system is restricted to offline hypothesis generation. Recommended Citation 33 and STARLI Research Works. Active Microrobotic Sampling for Embodied Biological Digital Twins at the Limit. Institute XXVIII, Extension 06, Version 1.0, 2026. Keywords biological digital twin; active sampling; microrobotics; expected information gain; Bayesian experimental design; organ on chip; model discrepancy; identifiability; quantum sensing; abstention; safe exploration; counterfactual replay; research gates", "publication_year": 2026, "cited_by_count": 0, "abstract_inverted_index": {"Active": [0, 86, 285], "Microrobotic": [1, 286], "Sampling": [2, 87, 287], "for": [3, 288], "Embod